            },
            "reviewBody": "Easy and delicious! This will be my \"go to\" recipe from now on!",
            "datePublished": "2016-01-26T12:10:32.090Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Amanda Spaugh Weekley"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this during a huge blizzard, when the store couldn't get and strawberries, but I liked how it mixed the stuff slowly, and used condensed milk, so I tried it without the strawberries. I mixed the extract and condensed milk together, then added 2-3 tablespoons of the mixture, 2 teaspoons of milk, and 2-3 cups of snow at a time, mixing well as I went. It had a good consistency, but it wasn't sweet enough, according to my 8 and 5 year old and my husband. So I added 5 tablespoons sugar and 3 tablespoons powdered sugar. It was really good then. I agree with them, it had a good vanilla taste, but it just wasn't sweet enough. The next time I make this, I'm going to use more condensed milk. My husband just said he'd give it 4 stars too.",
            "datePublished": "2016-01-23T18:13:03.567Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kristy Johnson"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was very good. I rated it a four because I had to add more strawberry to give it a better flavor. FYI, the regular milk is definitely needed; it gives it a better flavor than just the condensed milk. Overall, it really is a nice recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2013-03-25T07:43:20.430Z"
          },
